♪ By the dawn's early light ♪

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:25.834
("The Star-Spangled Banner")

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:27.751
- This is embarrassing.

00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:30.359
(laughs)

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:32.235
- Uh, ya damn right I've seen the video of

00:00:32.235 --> 00:00:35.142
Fergie singin' the national anthem.

00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:37.403
- I read about it on Twitter,

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.476
like, oh, you have to see this.

00:00:38.476 --> 00:00:40.106
- I feel so bad for her.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.391
I think she's singing
and she's like, whoa,

00:00:42.391 --> 00:00:43.717
I think she just got carried away.

00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:46.658
- But, you know, the
national anthem is arguably

00:00:46.658 --> 00:00:49.908
the most publicly performed thing ever.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:53.199
- Who rearranges the national anthem?

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:55.950
You just have to be so...Fergie.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.289
- I think you can add
a little bit musically,

00:00:58.289 --> 00:00:59.453
but what she did was almost just

00:00:59.453 --> 00:01:01.122
like changing the emotion or the mood.

00:01:01.122 --> 00:01:02.970
- She made a choice.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.143
She made that choice and she
stuck with it the whole time.

00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:09.227
- I just don't know if it
worked out this way, you know?

00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:11.538
- Fergie is always going
to be Fergalicious,

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.621
and I believe that, but
the way that she sang it,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.439
I think they called it jazzy.

00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:21.360
- We never heard the first
person sing the national anthem,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.540
so, sure, go ahead,
that doesn't bother me.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.476
- You know, it's cool.

00:01:25.476 --> 00:01:26.474
It's cool to mix it up.

00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:28.724
(drumroll)

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:31.382
- No.
(laughs)

00:01:31.382 --> 00:01:32.757
I'm scared now.

00:01:32.757 --> 00:01:34.006
- Like Fergie sings it?

00:01:34.006 --> 00:01:34.839
'Cause I can't.

00:01:34.839 --> 00:01:36.069
I can't even come close.

00:01:36.069 --> 00:01:38.922
She's like a diamond in the sky.

00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:40.942
- Umm, that's a no.

00:01:40.942 --> 00:01:42.094
- Not at all.

00:01:42.094 --> 00:01:43.194
Not in the least.

00:01:43.194 --> 00:01:44.033
Absolutely not.

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.511
- I mean, I will sing the
national anthem right now,

00:01:46.511 --> 00:01:47.634
but I'm also scared.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.113
- I'm down to sing the national anthem.

00:01:49.113 --> 00:01:50.578
- Yeah, I'd be down to give it a try.

00:01:50.578 --> 00:01:54.048
- I am so confident and ready
to sing the national anthem.

00:01:54.048 --> 00:01:55.833
I'm literally the best singer ever.

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:59.504
- Yeah, I think I can sing it right now.

00:01:59.504 --> 00:02:01.095
- Vocal warm-up, okay.

00:02:01.095 --> 00:02:03.792
(sings vocal scale)

00:02:03.792 --> 00:02:05.928
(hums)
- I can't do that!

00:02:05.928 --> 00:02:08.507
("The Star-Spangled Banner")

00:02:08.507 --> 00:02:10.229
- Where's my pitch pipe?

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.062
People?

00:02:11.062 --> 00:02:12.542
Where's my pitch pipe?

00:02:12.542 --> 00:02:13.896
(laughs)

00:02:13.896 --> 00:02:15.017
- I'm so nervous.

00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:15.997
It's totally fine.

00:02:15.997 --> 00:02:16.830
I can start whenever?

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.981
- We'll just give it a go.
(laughs)

00:02:20.981 --> 00:02:25.981
♪ Oh, say can you see ♪

00:02:26.276 --> 00:02:29.872
♪ By the star's early light ♪

00:02:29.872 --> 00:02:33.800
♪ What so proudly we hailed ♪

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.982
♪ At the twilight's last gleaming ♪

00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:42.565
♪ Whose broad stripes and bright stars ♪

00:02:43.448 --> 00:02:45.276
- Oh my God, I'm so nervous!

00:02:45.276 --> 00:02:47.894
I was not nervous at all!

00:02:47.894 --> 00:02:48.890
How do people do this in front

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.897
